> Of course the corresponding argument is that you don't need a date 
> "system".  You just give the information someone wants, in the order that 
> they are likely to find it important given the context.

This procedure for finding this order is:  

1 identify the common outermost level between the speaker and the listener
2 go from the outside to the inside and try to use any shortcut that is
  available to both the speaker and the listener, e.g. "San Francisco"
  as a shortcut for "USA / CA / San Francisco"
 
